To read analog input into an array with a fixed sampling rate using Arduino, you can use the following code. This code continuously reads from analog channel 1 and stores the values in an array, ensuring a delay of 100ms between each sample. The sampling loop runs until the array is full.

```cpp
const int numSamples = 1000;
int samples[numSamples];
int sampleIndex = 0;

void setup() {
  Serial.begin(9600);
}

void loop() {
  if (sampleIndex < numSamples) {
    samples[sampleIndex] = analogRead(A1);
    sampleIndex++;
    delay(100);
  } else {
    // Array is full, do something with the data
    for (int i = 0; i < numSamples; i++) {
      Serial.println(samples[i]);
    }
  }
}
```

This code ensures that the analog input is sampled at a consistent rate and stored for further processing.
